  "body": "PR #348 (#300) adds tool-library export and import to the GUI's Tool library page. The undoable app commands are in `crates/app/src/commands/tool_import.rs`, and the file format is in `crates/app/src/tool_library.rs`. The MCP server (`camcraft-cli mcp`, #128) has no tool for either, so an agent can't save a document's tools to a library or load a library into a document.\n\n**Proposed**\n- `export_tool_library {path}`: writes the document's tools to a library file, in the same format as the GUI's Export.\n- `import_tool_library {path}`: imports through the same command as the GUI. Same rules: an identical tool is skipped, a clashing name arrives as \"Name (2)\", a malformed or insane file is refused by name, and the import is one undo step.\n- Optionally, matching job-script verbs in the script VERBS table and `assets/scripts/cam.d.ts`, so the batch lane and the MCP lane keep one meaning per verb (the #128 design).\n\n**Done means**\n- Both tools are listed by `tools/list`, with schemas.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs` covers an export → import roundtrip into a fresh document, a duplicate skip, a refusal of a malformed file, and undo/redo of the import.\n\nDepends on #348 merging. Part of #128.\n",
